ealed-visas/426-domestic-worker-temporary-diplomatic-and-consular-visa.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/repealed-visas/427-domestic-worker-temporary-executive-visa.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/repealed-visas/488-superyacht-crew-visa.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/work/187-direct-entry-stream.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/work/489-invited-pathway.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/repealed-visas/485-temporary-graduate-replacement-stream.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/repealed-visas/476-skilled-recognised-graduate.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/repealed-visas/medium-term-stream-482-repealed.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/repealed-visas/short-term-stream-482-repealed.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/repealed-visas/labour-stream-482-repealed.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/repealed-visas/confirmatory-residence-subclass-808.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/repealed-visas/business-owner-subclass-890-visa.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/repealed-visas/investor-subclass-891-visa.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/repealed-visas/state-or-territory-sponsored-business-owner-subclass-892-visa.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/repealed-visas/state-or-territory-sponsored-investor-subclass-893-visa.aspx"],"updateDate":"3/10/2025 10:00:18 AM"},{"title":"DFV 000 emergency banner","content":"\u003cp\u003eCall 000 if you are in immediate danger.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eFor 24/7 counselling and support, call 1800 737 732 to speak to \u003ca class=\u0027external\u0027 aria-label=\u00271800RESPECT - external link\u0027 href=\u0027https\u0026#58;//1800respect.org.au/\u0027\u003e1800RESPECT\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e​\u003cbr\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/supporting/Pages/Family/information-for-partner-visa-sponsors.aspx","/supporting/Pages/Family/service-providers.aspx","/supporting/Pages/Family/family-violence-provisions.aspx","/supporting/Pages/Family/family-violence-provisions-partner-visa-applicants.aspx","/supporting/Pages/Family/family-violence-provisions-secondary-applicants.aspx","/supporting/Pages/Family/domestic-family-violence-how-we-can-help-you.aspx","/form-listing/Pages/notification-of-family-violence-secondary-applicants.aspx","/supporting/Pages/Family/domestic-family-violence-and-your-visa.aspx","/supporting/Pages/dfv-contact-form.aspx","/supporting/Pages/Family/relationship-evidence.aspx","/supporting/Pages/Family/family-violence-evidence.aspx","/supporting/Pages/Family/types-of-domestic-and-family-violence.aspx","/supporting/Pages/Family/domestic-family-violence-where-to-get-help.aspx"],"updateDate":"28/07/2025 12:15:21 PM"},{"title":"New Zealand Citizen Family Relationship visa","content":"\u003cp\u003eWe strongly encourage you to undertake any required health examinations and character checks before lodging their application. Lodging a complete application assists with quicker processing times. See Step by Step – Gather your documents.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003eFrom 23 July 2025, applicants for New Zealand Citizen Family Relationship (subclass 461) visa applicants can import their paper application into ImmiAccount. For more information, see \u003ca href=\u0027/news-media/archive/article?itemId=1338\u0027\u003eUpdate to ImmiAccount — new online services for paper-based Child, Other Family, Former Residents, and New Zealand Citizen Family Relationship visa applications\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e​\u003cbr\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/Visa-subsite/Pages/family/461-new-zealand-citizen-family-relationship.aspx"],"updateDate":"25/07/2025 12:24:18 PM"},{"title":"Former Resident (subclass 151) ","content":"\u003cp\u003eFrom 23 July 2025, applicants for Former Resident (subclass 151) visa applicants can import their paper application into ImmiAccount. \u003cbr\u003eFor more information, see \u003ca href=\u0027/news-media/archive/article?itemId=1338\u0027\u003eUpdate to ImmiAccount — new online services for paper-based Child, Other Family, Former Residents, and New Zealand Citizen Family Relationship visa applications\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e​\u003cbr\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/Visa-subsite/Pages/other-visas/151-former-resident-visa.aspx"],"updateDate":"25/07/2025 12:24:01 PM"},{"title":"Other Family subclasses 114, 115, 116, 835, 836 and 838","content":"\u003cp\u003eFrom 23 July 2025, applicants for Other Family subclasses 114, 115, 116, 835, 836 and 838 can import their paper application into ImmiAccount. Some existing applications made outside of Australia before 25 June 2020 cannot be imported into ImmiAccount. \u003cbr\u003eFor more information, see \u003ca href=\u0027/news-media/archive/article?itemId=1338\u0027\u003eUpdate to ImmiAccount — new online services for paper-based Child, Other Family, Former Residents, and New Zealand Citizen Family Relationship visa applications\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e​\u003cbr\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/Visa-subsite/Pages/family/114-aged-dependent-relative.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/family/115-remaining-relative.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/family/116-carer-visa.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/family/835-remaining-relative-visa.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/family/836-carer-visa.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/family/838-aged-dependent-relative-visa.aspx"],"updateDate":"25/07/2025 12:23:34 PM"},{"title":"Child visa subclasses 101, 102, 802, 445, 117 and 837","content":"\u003cp\u003eFrom 23 July 2025, applicants for Child visa subclasses 101, 102, 802, 445, 117 and 837 can import their paper application into ImmiAccount. Some existing applications made outside of Australia before 1 April 2020 cannot be imported into ImmiAccount. \u003cbr\u003eFor more information, see \u003ca href=\u0027/news-media/archive/article?itemId=1338\u0027\u003eUpdate to ImmiAccount — new online services for paper-based Child, Other Family, Former Residents, and New Zealand Citizen Family Relationship visa applications\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e​\u003cbr\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/Visa-subsite/Pages/family/101-child-visa.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/family/102-adoption-visa.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/family/802-child-visa.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/family/445-dependent-child.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/family/117-orphan-relative.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/family/837-orphan-relative.aspx"],"updateDate":"25/07/2025 12:23:00 PM"},{"title":"PDF forms - 929","content":"\u003cp\u003e​From 25 November 2024, paper Form 929 - Change of contact and/or passport details will no longer be available to use. To find out how you can update your passport or contact details, visit \u003ca href=\u0027/change-in-situation\u0027\u003eC​hange in your situation\u003c/a\u003e.​​​\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/form-listing/Pages/Departmental-forms-listing/pdf-forms.aspx"],"updateDate":"9/07/2025 4:28:24 PM"},{"title":"Closure of subclasses 890, 891, 892, 892","content":"\u003cp\u003eThis visa closed to new applications on 21 March 2025. We will continue to process applications made before this date.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/Visa-subsite/Pages/work/890-business-owner.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/work/891-business-innovation-investment-permanent.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/work/892-state-territory-sponsored-business-owner.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/work/893-state-or-territory-sponsored-investor.aspx"],"updateDate":"6/05/2025 11:57:38 AM"},{"title":"188 stream closed to applications","content":"\u003cp\u003eThis stream closed to applications on 31 July 2024. We will continue to process applications made before this date. If you withdrew your application on or after 31 July 2024, a refund of the Visa Application Charge (VAC) is available. For details, visit the\u0026#160;\u003ca href=\u0027https\u0026#58;//immi.homeaffairs.gov.au/visas/getting-a-visa/biip-closure-and-refunds\u0027\u003eBIIP closure and refunds page.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e​​​\u003cbr\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/Visa-subsite/Pages/work/188-business-innovation-stream.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/work/188-investor.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/work/188-significant-investor-stream.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/work/188-entrepreneur-stream.aspx"],"updateDate":"7/03/2025 11:40:33 AM"},{"title":"132 visa closed to new applicants","content":"\u003cp\u003eThis stream closed to applications on 1 July 2021. We will continue to process applications made before this date. If you withdrew your application on or after 31 July 2024, a refund of the Visa Application Charge (VAC) is available. For details, visit the\u0026#160;\u003ca href=\u0027https\u0026#58;//immi.homeaffairs.gov.au/visas/getting-a-visa/biip-closure-and-refunds\u0027\u003eBIIP closure and refunds page.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e​​\u003cbr\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/Visa-subsite/Pages/work/132-significant-business-history.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/work/132-venture-capital-entrepreneur-stream.aspx"],"updateDate":"7/03/2025 11:33:12 AM"},{"title":"Table search - Refresh alert","content":"​\u003cp\u003eIf you experience problems loading this page, please clear your browser cache and refresh your browser (Ctrl and F5). If you continue to experience issues loading this page please submit feedback.\u003c/p\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/work-in-australia/Pages/Assessing-authorities.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/Processing-times/Visa-processing-times.aspx","/form-listing/Pages/Departmental-forms-listing/Online-forms.aspx","/employer-subsite/Pages/list-of-current-labour-agreements.aspx"],"updateDate":"19/02/2025 9:41:58 AM"},{"title":"Repealed visa - closure of pandemic 408","content":"\u003cp\u003eThis visa is closed to new applicants.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe COVID-19 Pandemic event visa closed to all applications on 1 February 2024. For more information, see ​\u003ca href=\u0027/news-media/archive/article?itemId=1169\u0027\u003eClosure of the Pandemic Event\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe will continue to assess all applications lodged before 1 February 2024.​​\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/Visa-subsite/Pages/repealed-visas/australian-government-endorsed-events-covid-19-pandemic-event-subclass-408.aspx"],"updateDate":"24/01/2025 9:55:25 AM"},{"title":"866 - Protection visa for asylum seekers","content":"\u003cp\u003eBig changes are here to stop people misusing protection visas. If you are thinking about applying for protection you can get \u003ca href=\u0027/visas/getting-a-visa/visa-listing/protection-866/genuine-asylum-seekers#content-index-3\u0027\u003efree legal advice\u003c/a\u003e. To find out if a Protection visa is right for you or someone you know try our \u003ca href=\u0027/visas/getting-a-visa/visa-listing/protection-866/what-you-need-to-know-866-visa\u0027\u003eonline tool\u003c/a\u003e. For more information, see \u003ca href=\u0027/visas/getting-a-visa/visa-listing/protection-866/genuine-asylum-seekers\u0027\u003eProtection visas are for genuine asylum seekers\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e​\u003cbr\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/Visa-subsite/Pages/refugee-and-humanitarian/866-protection-visa.aspx"],"updateDate":"23/01/2025 9:56:18 AM"},{"title":"Visitor visa - process app faster","content":"\u003cp\u003eFind out what you can do to\u0026#160;\u003ca href=\u0027/check-twice-submit-once\u0027 target=\u0027_blank\u0027\u003ehelp us process your application faster\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAustralian citizens are ineligible to apply for an eVisitor visa, refer to\u0026#160;\u003ca href=\u0027https\u0026#58;//immi.homeaffairs.gov.au/entering-and-leaving-australia/entering-australia/crossing-the-border/travel-documents-for-australian-citizens-and-permanent-residents\u0027\u003eEntering Australia\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e​\u003cbr\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/Visa-subsite/Pages/visit/651-evisitor.aspx"],"updateDate":"10/01/2025 1:43:09 PM"},{"title":"Global Talent program","content":"\u003cp\u003eThe Global Talent visa​ is closed to new applications as of 6 December 2024. The National Innovation visa has replaced the Global Talent visa. We will continue to process on-hand Global Talent visa applications in accordance with processing priorities and annual migration planning levels.\u003c/p\u003e​ ","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/Visa-subsite/Pages/work/858-distinguished-talent.aspx"],"updateDate":"9/12/2024 2:46:43 PM"},{"title":"TSS repeal - short term","content":"\u003cp\u003eOn December 7 2024,\u0026#160;the Skills in Demand (SID) visa replaced the Temporary Skills Shortage (TSS) visa.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026#160;All TSS nominations and visa applications lodged prior to the implementation of the SID visa will be processed using the requirements in force at the time the application was lodged.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026#160;If your employer has lodged a TSS nomination and you have not lodged your associated TSS visa application before 7 December 2024, if the nomination is approved it will be deemed a SID nomination and you can lodge an associated application for a SID visa. If you hold a TSS visa, see \u003ca href=\u0027/visas/getting-a-visa/visa-listing/repealed-visas/temporary-skill-shortage-short-term-visa-subclass-482\u0027\u003eTemporary Skill Shortage (Short-term) visa (subclass 482)\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e​\u003cbr\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/Visa-subsite/Pages/work/482-core-skills-stream.aspx"],"updateDate":"6/12/2024 11:50:06 PM"},{"title":"TSS repeal - medium term","content":"\u003cp\u003eOn December 7 2024,\u0026#160;the Skills in Demand (SID) visa replaced the Temporary Skills Shortage (TSS) visa.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026#160;All TSS nominations and visa applications lodged prior to the implementation of the SID visa will be processed using the requirements in force at the time the application was lodged.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026#160;If your employer has lodged a TSS nomination and you have not lodged your associated TSS visa application before 7 December 2024, if the nomination is approved it will be deemed a SID nomination and you can lodge an associated application for a SID visa. If you hold a TSS visa, see \u003ca href=\u0027/visas/getting-a-visa/visa-listing/repealed-visas/temporary-skill-shortage-medium-term-visa-subclass-482\u0027\u003eTemporary Skill Shortage (Medium-term) visa (subclass 482)\u003c/a\u003e.​\u003c/p\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/Visa-subsite/Pages/work/specialist-skills-stream.aspx"],"updateDate":"6/12/2024 11:49:55 PM"},{"title":"TSS repeal - labour agreement ","content":"\u003cp\u003eOn December 7 2024,\u0026#160;the Skills in Demand (SID) visa replaced the Temporary Skills Shortage (TSS) visa.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026#160;All TSS nominations and visa applications lodged prior to the implementation of the SID visa will be processed using the requirements in force at the time the application was lodged.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026#160;If your employer has lodged a TSS nomination and you have not lodged your associated TSS visa application before 7 December 2024, if the nomination is approved it will be deemed a SID nomination and you can lodge an associated application for a SID visa. If you hold a TSS visa, see \u003ca href=\u0027/visas/getting-a-visa/visa-listing/repealed-visas/temporary-skill-shortage-labour-agreement-visa-subclass-482\u0027\u003eTemporary Skill Shortage (Labour agreement) visa (subclass 482)\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e​\u003cbr\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/Visa-subsite/Pages/work/sid-labour-agreement-stream.aspx"],"updateDate":"6/12/2024 11:49:48 PM"},{"title":"TSS repeal","content":"\u003cp\u003eOn December 7 2024,\u0026#160;the Skills in Demand (SID) visa replaced the Temporary Skills Shortage (TSS) visa.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026#160;All TSS nominations and visa applications lodged prior to the implementation of the SID visa will be processed using the requirements in force at the time the application was lodged.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026#160;If your employer has lodged a TSS nomination and you have not lodged your associated TSS visa application before 7 December 2024, if the nomination is approved it will be deemed a SID nomination and you can lodge an associated application for a SID visa. If you hold a TSS visa, see \u003ca href=\u0027/visas/getting-a-visa/visa-listing#content-index-6\u0027\u003eRepealed visas\u003c/a\u003e.​\u003c/p\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/Visa-subsite/Pages/work/skills-in-demand-482-landing.aspx"],"updateDate":"6/12/2024 11:49:37 PM"},{"title":"PV wizard survey","content":"\u003cp\u003eWe are trialling this new tool to help you find the right information for your situation. Please help us improve by completing this \u003ca class=\u0027external\u0027 href=\u0027https\u0026#58;//dibpau.qualtrics.com/jfe/form/SV_cSA5KgqmSeUqbIO\u0027 aria-label=\u0027feedback survey - External link\u0027\u003efeedback survey\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e​​\u003cbr\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/protection-visa-subsite/Pages/pv-wizard/pv-wizard-version2.aspx"],"updateDate":"2/12/2024 1:43:41 PM"},{"title":"Changes in your situation - 929","content":"\u003cp\u003eFrom 25 November 2024, paper Form 929 - Change of contact and/or passport details will no longer be available to use. Click on Passport details have changed, or Personal details have changed below for mor​​e information on how you can update your details with us.\u003c/p\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/changes-situation-subsite/Pages/Changes-in-situation.aspx"],"updateDate":"27/11/2024 2:40:57 PM"},{"title":"Transit visa 771","content":"\u003cp\u003eIf you will be in Australia for less than 8 hours and you are not leaving the airport you may not need to apply for a visa before you travel.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eCheck if you are eligible to \u003ca href=\u0027/visas/getting-a-visa/visa-listing/transit-771/travellers-eligible-to-transit-without-visa\u0027\u003etransit without a visa\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e​\u003cbr\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/Visa-subsite/Pages/other-visas/771-transit-visa.aspx"],"updateDate":"4/11/2024 9:10:52 AM"},{"title":"Important changes to immigration medical examinations","content":"\u003cp\u003e​\u003ca href=\u0027/help-support/meeting-our-requirements/health/special-consideration-for-children\u0027\u003eSpecial consideration for children born and ordinarily resident in Australia\u003c/a\u003e that do not meet the health requirement under Public Interest Criteria 4005 and 4007 have come into effect on 16\u0026#160;October\u0026#160;2024.\u003c/p\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/supporting/Pages/Health-requirements/who-needs-health-examinations.aspx","/supporting/Pages/Health-requirements/Arranging-health-examinations.aspx","/supporting/Pages/Health-requirements/on-the-day-of-your-appointment.aspx","/supporting/Pages/Health-requirements/Health-requirements.aspx"],"updateDate":"16/10/2024 10:04:48 AM"},{"title":"Closure of the BIIP","content":"\u003cp\u003eThe Business Innovation and Investment Program (BIIP) is closed as of 31 July 2024. Applications made before this date will still be processed. You may be entitled to a refund of your Business Innovation and Investment (subclass 188) Visa Application Charge (VAC) for the Business Innovation, Investor, Significant Investor or Entrepreneur streams if you withdrew your application on or after 31 July 2024.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eFor more information see \u003ca href=\u0027/visas/getting-a-visa/biip-closure-and-refunds\u0027\u003eBIIP closure and refunds\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/Visa-subsite/Pages/work/188-business-innovation-investment-landing.aspx"],"updateDate":"27/09/2024 11:58:09 AM"},{"title":"Disclaimer - You had a baby","content":"\u003cp\u003eIf you have had a child you should tell us as soon as possible.\u003c/p\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/changes-situation-subsite/Pages/you-had-a-baby/You-had-a-baby.aspx"],"updateDate":"6/06/2024 10:24:18 AM"},{"title":"Skilled-Recognised Graduate subclass 476","content":"\u003cp\u003eThis visa has been capped and ceased, meaning no more visas will be granted. The government intends to close this category permanently from 1 July 2024. For more information, see ​\u003ca href=\u0027/visas/getting-a-visa/visa-listing/skilled-recognition-graduate-476#About\u0027\u003eApplications for this visa\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e​​\u003cbr\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/Visa-subsite/Pages/work/476-skilled-recognised-graduate.aspx"],"updateDate":"10/05/2024 4:28:16 PM"},{"title":"ETA-app","content":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr/\u003e   \u003cstrong\u003eImportant information about the ETA\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAll\u0026#160;\u003ca href=\u0027/visas/getting-a-visa/visa-listing/electronic-travel-authority-601#Eligibility\u0027\u003eETA-eligible passport holders\u003c/a\u003e must apply for an ETA using the Australian ETA app. For more information, see our\u0026#160;\u003ca href=\u0027/visas/getting-a-visa/visa-listing/electronic-travel-authority-601#HowTo\u0027\u003eStep by step guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003eIf you are unable to use the app, you can apply online through ImmiAccount for another visa that suits your needs.\u003cbr\u003eEuropean passport holders may be eligible for an\u0026#160;\u003ca href=\u0027/visas/getting-a-visa/visa-listing/evisitor-651\u0027\u003eeVisitor (subclass 651)\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAustralian citizens are ineligible to apply for an ETA, refer to\u0026#160;\u003ca href=\u0027https\u0026#58;//immi.homeaffairs.gov.au/entering-and-leaving-australia/entering-australia/crossing-the-border/travel-documents-for-australian-citizens-and-permanent-residents\u0027\u003eEntering Australia\u003c/a\u003e.​\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/Visa-subsite/Pages/visit/601-eta.aspx"],"updateDate":"28/03/2024 10:42:10 AM"},{"title":"visitor-600","content":"\u003cp\u003eFind out what you can do to\u0026#160;\u003ca href=\u0027/check-twice-submit-once\u0027 target=\u0027_blank\u0027\u003ehelp us process your application faster\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cbr/\u003e​\u003cbr\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/Visa-subsite/Pages/visit/600-tourist-apply-in-australia.aspx"],"updateDate":"28/03/2024 9:47:09 AM"},{"title":"Visa 500","content":"\u003cp\u003eFrom 23 March 2024 the \u003ca href=\u0027/news-media/archive/article?itemId=1187\u0027 target=\u0027_blank\u0027\u003eGenuine Student requirement\u003c/a\u003e replaces the Genuine Temporary Entrant (GTE) requirement for Student visas. Also, applications lodged for a Student or Temporary Graduate visa will be assessed under the \u003ca href=\u0027/news-media/archive/article?itemId=1188\u0027 target=\u0027_blank\u0027\u003eNew English Language Requirements\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e​​​​​\u003cbr\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/Visa-subsite/Pages/student/500-student.aspx"],"updateDate":"23/03/2024 12:25:02 AM"},{"title":"TPV/SHEV update","content":"\u003cp\u003eFree visa application assistance is available to people who are eligible to apply for a Resolution of Status (RoS) visa. If you hold a Temporary Protection visa (TPV) or Safe Haven Enterprise visa (SHEV) you can contact the legal service provider in your state or territory. For more information see the \u003cbr/\u003e   \u003ca href=\u0027/Visa-subsite/files/english-ros-factsheet.pdf\u0027\u003eRoS visa fact sheet\u003c/a\u003e.​​\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Department of Home Affairs does not charge a fee to fast-track a visa. If you are offered this service, it is a scam.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eT​o apply for a RoS, you must apply before your TPV or SHEV expires.  If your visa expires, you will become unlawful and may lose access to government services.​\u003c/p\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/Visa-subsite/Pages/other-visas/851-RoS.aspx"],"updateDate":"19/10/2023 9:04:16 AM"},{"title":"medical examination and chest x-ray","content":"\u003cp\u003eThe Australian Government is streamlining requirements for temporary visa applicants in Australia.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eOur systems are being updated to reflect the new policy and your ImmiAccount should be updated soon.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eCheck if you still need to \u003ca href=\u0027https\u0026#58;//immi.homeaffairs.gov.au/news-media/archive/article?itemId=970\u0027\u003eundertake a medical examination and chest x-ray\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e​\u003cbr\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/Visa-subsite/Pages/work/482-temporary-skill-shortage-landing.aspx"],"updateDate":"11/10/2023 11:29:31 AM"},{"title":"Important information about the Approved Destination Status (ADS) stream","content":"\u003cp\u003e \u003cbr/\u003e   \u003cstrong\u003eImportant information about the Approved Destination Status (ADS) stream​​\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThis visa stream is only for eligible citizens from the People’s Republic of China visiting Australia on a tour organised by an approved travel agent. You need to contact a registered Approved Destination Status scheme travel agent to ask for them to apply for this visa on your behalf. For further information see our ​\u003ca href=\u0027/visas/getting-a-visa/visa-listing/visitor-600/approved-destination-stream#HowTo\u0027\u003eStep by step guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eFind out what you can do to \u003ca href=\u0027/check-twice-submit-once\u0027\u003ehelp us process your application faster\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e​\u003cbr\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/Visa-subsite/Pages/visit/600-approved-destination-status.aspx"],"updateDate":"25/09/2023 10:32:52 AM"},{"title":"Visas for GPs program","content":"\u003cp\u003eThe Visas for GPs program will cease on 16 September 2023, removing the requirement for employers of International Medical Graduates (IMGs) to apply for a Health Workforce Certificate (HWC).\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eFor more information on this change see ​\u003ca href=\u0027/news-media/archive/article?itemId=1111\u0027 target=\u0027_blank\u0027\u003eMaking it easier to hire overseas trained doct​ors to work in Australia\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e​","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/programs-subsite/Pages/skilled-migration-program/visas-for-gps-initiative-.aspx"],"updateDate":"28/08/2023 8:29:31 AM"},{"title":"Travel movement record","content":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAll Citizenship by Conferral applicants\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWe are receiving a higher than usual number of requests for international movement records. When entering your travel dates, dates of first arrival or visa grant dates, an estimated date will be accepted and a processing officer will confirm exact dates within our systems as required after you lodge your application. See \u003ca href=\u0027https\u0026#58;//immi.homeaffairs.gov.au/citizenship/become-a-citizen/permanent-resident\u0027\u003eBecome an Australian citizen (by conferral) Permanent residents or New Zealand citizens\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e​\u003cbr\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/form-listing/Pages/request-for-international-movement-records.aspx","/entering-leaving-subsite/Pages/Requesting-travel-records.aspx","/entering-leaving-subsite/Pages/apply.aspx","/entering-leaving-subsite/Pages/document-checklists.aspx","\r\n\r\n"],"updateDate":"24/07/2023 2:42:16 PM"},{"title":"189 visa permanently closed to new applications on 1 July 2023","content":"\u003cp\u003eThe Skilled Independent (subclass 189) (New Zealand stream) visa permanently closed to new applications on 1 July 2023. For more information see \u003ca href=\u0027/what-we-do/skilled-migration-program/recent-changes\u0027\u003eRecent changes\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cbr/\u003e​\u003cbr\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/Visa-subsite/Pages/work/189-skilled-independent-landing.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/work/189-new-zealand-stream.aspx\r\n"],"updateDate":"4/07/2023 2:52:30 PM"},{"title":"189 visa permanently closed to new applications on 1 July 2023 - 2nd version","content":"\u003cp\u003eThe Skilled Independent (subclass 189) (New Zealand stream) visa permanently closed to new applications on 1 July 2023. For more information see \n   \u003ca href=\u0027/what-we-do/skilled-migration-program/recent-changes\u0027\u003eRecent changes\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e ​\u003cbr\u003e​\u003cbr\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/Visa-subsite/Pages/work/189-new-zealand-stream.aspx"],"updateDate":"4/07/2023 2:52:22 PM"},{"title":"189 visa landing page","content":"\u003cp\u003eThe Skilled Independent (subclass 189) (New Zealand stream) visa is currently closed to new applications and will permanently close to new applications on 1 July 2023. For more information see \u003ca href=\u0027https\u0026#58;//immi.homeaffairs.gov.au/what-we-do/skilled-migration-program/recent-changes\u0027\u003eRecent changes\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e​\u003cbr\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/Visa-subsite/Pages/work/189-skilled-independent-landing.aspx"],"updateDate":"22/06/2023 3:41:18 PM"},{"title":"changes to immigration medical examinations","content":"\u003cp\u003eWe expect important changes to immigration medical examinations to come into effect on 1 July 2023. From this date urine tests will no longer form part of the medical examination. We will require a blood test to be undertaken instead. Applicants aged 15 years or older who have not completed their medical examinations prior to 1 July 2023 will no longer undertake a urine test. We will require them to undertake a blood test instead. We will no longer require children between the ages of 5 and 14 years old to undertake urine or blood tests unless clinically indicated.\u003c/p\u003e​\u003cbr\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/supporting/Pages/Health-requirements/who-needs-health-examinations.aspx","/supporting/Pages/Health-requirements/Health-requirements.aspx"],"updateDate":"30/05/2023 9:07:59 AM"},{"title":"fast track process- shev","content":"\u003cp\u003eCertain TPV holders and former holders may be eligible to apply for a permanent\u0026#160;\u003ca href=\u0027/visas/getting-a-visa/visa-listing/resolution-of-status-851\u0027 target=\u0027_blank\u0027\u003eResolution of Status (RoS) visa (subclass 851)\u003c/a\u003e.​​​​\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eOnly TPV and SHEV holders who first arrived in Australia on or after 14 February 2023 are eligible to apply for a subsequent TPV or SHEV.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/supporting/Pages/tpv-shev-in-language/overview.aspx"],"updateDate":"14/02/2023 2:24:02 PM"},{"title":"482 Temp shortage survey","content":"\u003cp\u003eThe Australian Government is streamlining requirements for temporary visa applicants in Australia.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eOur systems are being updated to reflect the new policy and your ImmiAccount should be updated soon.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eCheck if you still need to\u0026#160;\u003ca href=\u0027/news-media/archive/article?itemId=970\u0027\u003eundertake a medical examination and chest x-ray\u003c/a\u003e.​\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/Visa-subsite/Pages/work/482-temporary-skill-shortage-landing.aspx"],"updateDate":"21/12/2022 1:36:57 PM"},{"title":"WHM-Covid-19","content":"\u003cp\u003eProcessing of COVID-19 Pandemic event visa applications is being streamlined. If you applied for a COVID-19 Pandemic event visa and your application remains undecided, but you no longer wish to be granted this visa, you \u003cbr/\u003e   \u003cstrong\u003emust\u003c/strong\u003e withdraw your application as soon as possible. You can withdraw your application by submitting \u003cbr/\u003e   \u003cstrong\u003eForm 1446 Withdrawal of a visa application \u003c/strong\u003evia \u003cbr/\u003e   \u003ca class=\u0027external\u0027 href=\u0027https\u0026#58;//online.immi.gov.au/lusc/login\u0027 target=\u0027_blank\u0027\u003eImmiAccount\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Australian Government is streamlining requirements for temporary visa applicants in Australia.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eOur systems are being updated to reflect the new policy and your ImmiAccount should be updated soon.​\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eCheck if you still need to \u003ca href=\u0027https\u0026#58;//immi.homeaffairs.gov.au/news-media/archive/article?itemId=970\u0027\u003eundertake a medical examination and chest x-ray\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/Visa-subsite/Pages/work/408-Australian-government-endorsed-events-covid-19.aspx"],"updateDate":"4/11/2022 4:01:03 PM"},{"title":"Online lodgement webform availability from 1 August 2022","content":"\u003cp\u003e​​​From 1 August 2022, the option to apply for a Bridging visa A (BVA), B (BVB) and C (BVC) in-person or via a paper form will no longer be available.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eApplications for a Bridging visa A, B or C mu​​st be made online via ImmiAccount or the \u003ca href=\u0027/help-support/departmental-forms/online-forms/bridging-a-b-c-visa-application-online\u0027\u003eonline webform\u003c/a\u003e​.​\u003c/p\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/Visa-subsite/Pages/other-visas/010-bridging-visa-a.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/other-visas/030-bridging-visa-c.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/other-visas/020-bridging-visa-b.aspx"],"updateDate":"1/08/2022 8:14:19 AM"},{"title":"188 Premium Investor stream - closed","content":"\u003cp\u003e​This stream is closed to new applications\u003c/p\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/Visa-subsite/Pages/work/188-premium-investor-stream.aspx"],"updateDate":"30/06/2021 11:58:12 PM"},{"title":"subclass-124-closed","content":"This visa is closed to new applications. To apply for the Distinguished Tale​​nt visa see\u0026#160;\u003ca href=\u0027/visas/getting-a-visa/visa-listing/distinguished-talent-858\u0027\u003eGlobal Talent visa (subclass 858)\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026#160; ​\u003cbr\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/Visa-subsite/Pages/work/124-distinguished-talent.aspx"],"updateDate":"27/02/2021 11:37:54 AM"},{"title":"191 alert","content":"\u003cp\u003e\n   \u003cstrong\u003eThis visa does not commence until 16 November 2022.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eMore details will be provided in due course.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/Visa-subsite/Pages/work/191-permanent-residence.aspx"],"updateDate":"1/11/2019 3:03:36 PM"},{"title":"Beta - working in Australia","content":"\u003cp\u003eWe are working to improve the layout and content of this page.\u0026#160;Please ensure you review the \n   \u003ca href=\u0027/Pages/Conditions-of-use.aspx\u0027\u003econditions of use\u003c/a\u003e\u0026#160;as this content is under development. We welcome your feedback to help us improve the user experience. In the meantime, further information about your topic can be found \n   \u003ca class=\u0027external\u0027 href=\u0027https\u0026#58;//archive.homeaffairs.gov.au/trav/work\u0027 target=\u0027_blank\u0027\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/work-in-australia/Pages/Overview.aspx"],"updateDate":"16/10/2019 2:01:31 PM"},{"title":"Beta - WIA - Workplace rights","content":"\u003cp\u003eWe are working to improve the layout and content of this page.\u0026#160;Please ensure you review the \n   \u003ca href=\u0027/Pages/Conditions-of-use.aspx\u0027\u003econditions of use\u003c/a\u003e\u0026#160;as this content is under development. We welcome your feedback to help us improve the user experience. In the meantime, further information about your topic can be found \n   \u003ca class=\u0027external\u0027 href=\u0027https\u0026#58;//archive.homeaffairs.gov.au/trav/work/work/workplace-rights\u0027 target=\u0027_blank\u0027\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/work-in-australia/Pages/work-restrictions.aspx"],"updateDate":"2/04/2019 9:22:18 AM"},{"title":"Beta - Bringing Someone","content":"\u003cp\u003eWe are working to improve the layout and content of this page.\u0026#160;Please ensure you review the \n   \u003ca href=\u0027/Pages/Conditions-of-use.aspx\u0027\u003econditions of use\u003c/a\u003e\u0026#160;as this content is under development. We welcome your feedback to help us improve the user experience. In the meantime, further information about your topic can be found at \n   \u003ca class=\u0027external\u0027 href=\u0027https\u0026#58;//archive.homeaffairs.gov.au/trav/visa-1/408-\u0027 target=\u0027_blank\u0027\u003eTemporary Activity visa (subclass 408)\u003c/a\u003e, \n   \u003ca class=\u0027external\u0027 href=\u0027https\u0026#58;//archive.homeaffairs.gov.au/trav/visa-1/403-\u0027 target=\u0027_blank\u0027\u003eTemporary Work (International Relations) visa (subclass 403)\u003c/a\u003e or \n   \u003ca href=\u0027/visas/getting-a-visa/visa-listing/training-407\u0027 target=\u0027_blank\u0027\u003eTraining visa (subclass 407)\u003c/a\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/bringing/Pages/Overview.aspx","/bringing/Pages/Becoming-a-temporary-activities-sponsor.aspx","/bringing/Pages/Eligibility.aspx","/bringing/Pages/Obligations.aspx","/bringing/Pages/Step-by-step.aspx","/bringing/Pages/Sponsoring-and-supporting.aspx","/bringing/Pages/Sponsoring-an-applicant.aspx","/bringing/Pages/Supporting-an-applicant.aspx","/bringing/Pages/When-you-are-a-sponsor.aspx"],"updateDate":"20/12/2018 10:11:35 AM"},{"title":"Repealed 405 - 410","content":"\u003cp\u003eThis visa is closed to new applicants\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Pathway to permanent residence for retirement visa holders announced by Government as part of the 2018-19 Budget commenced on 17 November 2018.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eFurther details, including eligibility requirements, processing times and visa application charges can be found at\u0026#160;\u003ca href=\u0027/visas/permanent-resident/visa-options#content-index-3\u0027\u003ePathway to permanent residence for Retirees\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","type":"Page","category":"","urls":["/Visa-subsite/Pages/repealed-visas/405-investor-retirement-visa.aspx","/Visa-subsite/Pages/repealed-visas/410-retirement-visa.aspx"],"updateDate":"21/11/2018 9:55:12 AM"}],"glossaryTerms":[{"id":91,"title":"Accredited community language","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass6ABC64303BD849D79B54DBE5D4C8F7B8\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou must have been accredited at the paraprofessional level or above for interpreting or translating in a language they offer accreditation in by the\u0026#160;\u003ca href=\"http\u0026#58;//www.naati.com.au/\" class=\"external\" target=\"_blank\"\u003eNational Accreditation Authority for Translators and Interpreters\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Accredited-community-language"},{"id":106,"title":"Actively operating ","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClassD68040E4E6564F568C04E3D76B087B1E\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eFor a main business to be assessed as actively operating the applicant must provide evidence of business activity of a repetitive, continuous and permanent nature.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Actively-operating-"},{"id":97,"title":"Adult Migrant English Language Program (AMEP) ","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass1EAAF323DC4B4A58AB29079C416AB677\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e​The Adult Migrant English Language Program (AMEP) provides up to 510 hours of free English language tuition to eligible migrants from the skilled, family and humanitarian visa streams, to help them learn basic English to assist with their settlement in Australia. For further information about the AMEP, visit \r\n      \u003ca href=\"https\u0026#58;//immi.homeaffairs.gov.au/settling-in-australia/amep/about-the-program\"\u003eAdult Migrant English Program\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Adult-Migrant-English-Language-Program-(AMEP)-"},{"id":56,"title":"Adverse information","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClassF7EC4447C86943D986B35965116358CC\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e Adverse information is unfavourable information that could impact on your suitability as an approved sponsor.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":true,"hash":"Adverse-information"},{"id":38,"title":"Annual income","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass346A5279410D4B7FA8637C2FFD0F41B1\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eAnnual income means\u0026#160;how much money you make in a year. See details on what you can include as an evidence of annual income.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":true,"hash":"Annual-income"},{"id":3,"title":"Applicant","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClassB39D709B95AF4A37A059836CCBEB0D40\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e​An applicant is\u0026#160;a person who is applying for a visa or for citizenship.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Applicant"},{"id":11,"title":"Biometrics","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass333CCF71A4E242BAB43B7A1C1A7DCCBD\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eBiometrics are features of your body that can be used to identify you. They include\u0026#58;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003efingerprints\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ean image of your face\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe might collect your biometrics\u0026#160;during the application process for a visa, or for other services.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThese biometrics are types of ‘personal identifiers’, a term used in the \u003cem\u003eMigration Act 1958\u003c/em\u003e, the \u003cem\u003eMigration Regulations 1994\u003c/em\u003e and the \u003cem\u003eAustralian Citizenship Act 2007\u003c/em\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e​\r\n         \u003ca href=\"/help-support/meeting-our-requirements/biometrics\"\u003eSee details\u003c/a\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Biometrics"},{"id":107,"title":"Bogus documents","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass1266667794784BB090B54081997FD069\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eA document that the Minister reasonably suspects is a document that\u0026#58;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n   \u003cli\u003epurports to have been, but was not, issued in respect of the person, or\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e is counterfeit or has been altered by a person who does not have authority to do so, or\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e was obtained because of a false or misleading statement, whether or not made knowingly\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Bogus-documents"},{"id":121,"title":"British subject","definition":"\u003cp\u003e​Includes a person who was, immediately prior to the date of commencement of this Act, entitled in Australia or a Territory to all political and other rights, powers and privileges to which a natural-born British subject was then entitled.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"British-subject"},{"id":1,"title":"Business visitor activities","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass2EAE7BD504A54C058AD269A9BA341F99\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eA business visitor can\u0026#58;\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cdiv\u003emake general business or employment enquiries\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cdiv\u003einvestigate, negotiate, sign or review a business contract\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cdiv\u003eundertake an activity as part of\u0026#160;an official government visit\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cdiv\u003etake part in a conference, trade fair or seminar. The organisers cannot pay you to take part\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eBusiness visitors cannot\u0026#58;\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003ework for or provide services to a person, business or organisation\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003esell goods or services to the public\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Business-visitor-activities"},{"id":76,"title":"Cap and cease","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClassF9911375867441F891E7C4B7556F00D6\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eCap and cease means when a cap has been reached for a particular visa class\u0026#58;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003ework on all applications which have not been processed to decision stops\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ethe files are closed\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eapplication fees are refunded\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eThese applications are treated as if they have not been submitted.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Cap-and-cease"},{"id":46,"title":"Capping and queueing","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass08033B112FE04D1BB9DADA20E14FFA18\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eCapping means a limited number of the visa will be granted each \r\n      \u003ca href=\"/help-support/glossary?expand=true#migration-program-year\"\u003eMigration Program\u0026#160;year\u003c/a\u003e. Once we reach this number, no more visas will be granted that year.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e ​\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":true,"hash":"Capping-and-queueing"},{"id":4,"title":"Certified copy","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass7CFD13674D9C43E786A4EA94789305BB\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eA certified copy is a copy of an original document that has been confirmed to be a true copy of the document by an authorised person.\u0026#160;\u003ca href=\"/help-support/applying-online-or-on-paper/on-paper/certified-copy\"\u003eSee in details\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Certified-copy"},{"id":74,"title":"Child","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass9C7D47865A3D4FEEBBCB386BBDF666D7\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eYour child is your\u0026#58;\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003ebiological child\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\r\n         \u003ca href=\"/help-support/glossary?expand=true#stepchild\"\u003estepchild\u003c/a\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eadopted child​\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Child"},{"id":68,"title":"De facto","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass18CE322B4572498F935C6929E5459CF7\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eA de facto relationship is one where you and your partner are not legally married to each other\u0026#160;but\u0026#58;\u0026#160;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eyou are committed to a shared life excluding\u0026#160;all others; and\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eyour relationship is genuine and continuing; and\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eyou live together; \u003cstrong\u003eor \u003c/strong\u003edo not live separately and apart on a permanent basis; and\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eyou are not related by family.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cdiv\u003eA de facto relationship can be with someone of the same or different sex.​\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":true,"hash":"De-facto"},{"id":75,"title":"Dependant","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass2B277C7E80884F659BEDA33825A66839\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eA dependant is\u0026#58;\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003esomeone who has wholly or substantially\u0026#160;relied on mostly you for a substantial\u0026#160;period of time to meet their basic needs of food, clothing and shelter\u0026#160;\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003esomeone who has wholly or substantially\u0026#160;relied on you for a substantial period of time for financial support because they can\u0027t work due to a mental or physical disability\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Dependant"},{"id":43,"title":"Dependent child","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClassD31976D346F740138DA53A834BC38CD4\"\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cp\u003eSome visas allow you to include a dependent child in your application. \u0026#160;See details\u0026#160;to see if a child qualifies\u0026#160;to be a dependent child.\u0026#160;\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":true,"hash":"Dependent-child"},{"id":20,"title":"DNA testing","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass93DDF0DB29A9495699273C59488084A1\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eDNA (deoxyribonucleic acid)\u0026#160;testing compares genetic material from 2 or more people to see if they are biologically related.\u0026#160;DNA\u0026#160;test results can prove a biological relationship exists. For example, between a parent and child, or siblings.\u0026#160; Usually genetic material from a mouth swab or blood sample is tested.​\u003c/p\u003e\r\n   \u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/div\u003e​\u003cbr\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"DNA-testing"},{"id":119,"title":"Eligible investments","definition":"\u003cp\u003eMust be owned for the purpose of producing a return in the form of income or capital gain, and not for personal use and is one or more of the following\u0026#58;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003ean ownership interest in a business\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ecash on deposit\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003estocks or bonds\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ereal estate\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003egold or silver bullion​\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Eligible-investments"},{"id":35,"title":"Eligible New Zealand citizen","definition":"\u003cp\u003eAn eligible New Zealand citizen is a New Zealand citizen who is a protected SCV (Special Category visa – subclass 444) holder within the meaning of section 7 of the \r\n   \u003cem\u003e​\u003ca class=\"external\" href=\"https\u0026#58;//www.legislation.gov.au/Series/C2004A04121\" target=\"_blank\"\u003eSocial Security Act 1991\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/em\u003e (SSA). You are a protected SCV holder at a particular time, if you\u0026#58;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003ewere physically in Australia on 26 February 2001 as the holder of an\u0026#160;SCV\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ewere not in Australia on 26 February 2001 but were in Australia for 365 days (or more) between 26 February 1999 and 25 February 2001 (inclusive) and returned to Australia after 26 February 2001, or\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eare otherwise a ‘protected SCV holder’ under section 7(2B), 7(2C) or 7(2D) of the \u003ca class=\"external\" href=\"https\u0026#58;//www.legislation.gov.au/Series/C2004A04121\" target=\"_blank\"\u003eSSA\u003c/a\u003e - in which case you must provide us with written confirmation from Centrelink that you are a protected SCV holder​.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e​\u003cbr\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Eligible-New-Zealand-citizen"},{"id":116,"title":"Eligible student visa","definition":"\u003cp\u003eAn eligible student visa\u0026#160;is a student visa\u0026#160;other than a\u0026#58;\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003col type=\"a\"\u003e\u003cli\u003evisa granted to a\u0026#160;\u003ca href=\"https\u0026#58;//legend.border.gov.au/migration/2017-2020/2020/15-08-2021/regs/Pages/_document00000/_level%20100001/_level%20200001/level%20200002.aspx\"\u003eForeign Affairs student\u003c/a\u003e\u0026#160;or\u0026#160;\u003ca href=\"https\u0026#58;//legend.border.gov.au/migration/2017-2020/2020/15-08-2021/regs/Pages/_document00000/_level%20100001/level%20200001.aspx\"\u003eDefence Student\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003evisa granted on the basis of the applicant being a\u0026#160;\u003ca href=\"https\u0026#58;//legend.border.gov.au/Migration/2017-2020/2020/15-08-2021/acts/Pages/_document00000/level%20100002.aspx#JD_5-memberofthefamilyunit\"\u003emember of the family unit\u003c/a\u003e\u0026#160;of the holder of a\u0026#160;\u003ca href=\"https\u0026#58;//legend.border.gov.au/migration/2017-2020/2020/15-08-2021/regs/Pages/_document00000/_level%20100001/_level%20200001/level%20200002.aspx#JD_103-studentvisa\"\u003estudent visa\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ol\u003e​\u003cbr\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Eligible-student-visa"},{"id":31,"title":"Employer","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass6CE8D7F2066348728453B81180874E99\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eYour employer is the person or an organisation that pays you to do work for them.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe identify employers by their Australian Business Number (ABN).\u003c/p\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Employer"},{"id":115,"title":"False and misleading","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass7AB8A75263DB4EBBB86AA1D716497FF7\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eInformation that is false or misleading in a material particular means information that is\u0026#58;\u0026#160;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003efalse or misleading at the time it is given and\u0026#160;\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003erelevant to any of the criteria the Minister may consider when making a decision on an application, whether or not the decision is made because of that information \u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"False-and-misleading"},{"id":100,"title":"Finally determined","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass753B8B5944A8460A8C357D06DB669EB8\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe meaning of finally determined depends on your merits review rights\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n   \r\n\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":true,"hash":"Finally-determined"},{"id":114,"title":"Financial institution","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass403255E7A94F4D98890A57FC85569143\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eA body corporate that, as part of its normal activities, takes money on deposit and makes advances of money\u0026#58;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eunder a regulatory regime\u0026#58;\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003egoverned by the central bank (or its equivalent) of the country in which the body corporate operates; and\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ethat the Minister is satisfied provides effective prudential assurance; and\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cli\u003ein a way that the Minister is satisfied complies with effective prudential assurance requirements.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\n  \u003cbr\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Financial-institution"},{"id":55,"title":"Former relationships","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClassE520CEB648814E82AAAD28A2DB9DD047\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eA former relationship is a previous marriage or de facto partnership.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":true,"hash":"Former-relationships"},{"id":49,"title":"HAP ID","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClassAACA384D478A4EC084F55137B8C58448\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe HAP is a health case identifier (HAP ID) for eMedical, our electronic health processing system.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":true,"hash":"HAP-ID"},{"id":103,"title":"Immigration clearance","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass8205EE5B224747B2A624B56D0EEA152D\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eWhen you arrive in Australia you will be in immigration clearance. Your identity and travel documents will be checked by a clearance authority as part of the immigration clearance process.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOnce the clearance authority confirms your identity and that you hold a valid visa, you are formally allowed to enter Australia.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou might be refused entry to Australia if you don\u0027t meet immigration clearance requirements.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Immigration-clearance"},{"id":25,"title":"Immigration detention","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass5A4B791038EA48DAAB9FFED7039F9339\"\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cp\u003e We can detain you under the Migration Act 1958 if you are here unlawfully.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Immigration-detention"},{"id":17,"title":"International surrogacy","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass395643191ED34F9B901853585629DC74\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eInternational surrogacy is an arrangement between commissioning parents in Australia and a surrogate mother who lives in an another country. \u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":true,"hash":"International-surrogacy"},{"id":27,"title":"Judicial review","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClassEEEB8B2B547B476A9BCB4D18FFF85918\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eJudicial review is when a court reviews how a decision was made. This is to determine if there were any legal errors that could lead to the decision being invalid.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Judicial-review"},{"id":26,"title":"Long-term partner relationship","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass4D97C6E53BF84DACAE2265C8196A16CE\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou are in a long-term partner relationship if you and another person have been in a relationship, each as the \r\n      \u003ca href=\"/help-support/glossary?expand=true#spouse\"\u003espouse\u003c/a\u003e or \r\n      \u003ca href=\"/help-support/glossary?expand=true#defacto\"\u003ede facto\u003c/a\u003e partner of the other, that has continued\u0026#58;​\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003efor not less than 2 years and there is a \r\n         \u003ca href=\"/help-support/glossary?expand=true#dependentchild\"\u003edependent child\u003c/a\u003e (other than a \r\n         \u003ca href=\"/help-support/glossary?expand=true#stepchild\"\u003estep-child\u003c/a\u003e) from this relationship, or\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ein any other case, for not less than 3 years\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\r\n      \u003cbr\u003e\r\n   \u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":true,"hash":"Long-term-partner-relationship"},{"id":110,"title":"Main business","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass14A2EE3FB400422BAB6D8AAAFBEAA42A\"\u003e\n   \u003cp\u003eYou can nominate a main business that you actively operate for profit by providing goods and services to the public.\u0026#160; You must demonstrate an acceptable level of ownership in the business and direct involvement in its operations, you may also need to provide evidence of business turnover.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":true,"hash":"Main-business"},{"id":65,"title":"Medical Officer of the Commonwealth","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass6755FA11397E4DE0926851A690936127\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eA medical Officer of the Commonwealth (MOC) is a registered medical practitioner appointed by the Department of Home Affairs. They assess whether applicants meet the health requirements under the Migration Regulations 1994. They may work directly for the Department, or be employed by the Migration Medical Services Provider.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Medical-Officer-of-the-Commonwealth"},{"id":54,"title":"Members of the family unit","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass0471FD778D3D4DE3914496CB0213A826\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eFor general\u0026#160;visa purposes, you are a member of the main applicant\u0027s family unit if you are\u0026#58;\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003ethe main applicant\u0027s spouse or de facto partner\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ethe main applicant\u0027s \r\n         \u003ca href=\"/help-support/glossary?expand=true#child\"\u003echild\u003c/a\u003e, or their part​ner\u0027s child, who is\u0026#160;not engaged, married or in a de facto relationship and is\u0026#58;\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eaged under 18 years\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eaged 18 to 23 years\u0026#160;and dependent on the main applicant or the main applicant\u0027s partner\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eaged 23 years\u0026#160;or older and dependent on the main applicant or the main applicant\u0027s partner due to a partial or total physical or mental disability.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cli\u003ethe dependent \r\n         \u003ca href=\"/help-support/glossary?expand=true#child\"\u003echild\u003c/a\u003e of the child above\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003e\r\n      \u003cstrong\u003eNote\u0026#58;\u003c/strong\u003e the main applicant’s parent are not considered a member of the family unit.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eFor certain visas, you may be required to be a member of the family unit of a person who is not the main applicant.\u003c/p\u003e​ \u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Members-of-the-family-unit"},{"id":84,"title":"Migration Program year","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClassE925BF20032241B28EC13EB6ECDCB936\"\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cp\u003eAustralia\u0027s Migration Program is set annually. The Migration Program year, like the Australian financial year, runs from 1 July to 30 June.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Migration-Program-year"},{"id":127,"title":"Mistake was made by the applicant","definition":"\u003cp\u003eFor a refund of a visa application charge - a mistake made by the applicant is when the applicant has\u0026#58;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eapplied for the wrong visa class and/or visa stream, or\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eindicated the wrong visa duration in the visa application process, and\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ewe have received a new application.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e","ismoredetails":true,"hash":"Mistake-was-made-by-the-applicant"},{"id":126,"title":"Mistake was made by the department","definition":"\u003cp\u003eFor a refund of a visa application charge - mistake made by the department is where advice given by the department has led the applicant to apply for a visa that\u0026#58;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003ethey did not need\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ethey did not, or would not, be eligible for\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ewas the wrong type of visa, or\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ewas a system error at time of lodgement.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","ismoredetails":true,"hash":"Mistake-was-made-by-the-department"},{"id":57,"title":"Near relative","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass80E2C19529BF482AB3830B570C2EDF5C\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eFor remaining relative visas, your near relative is your\u0026#58;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eparent or step-parent\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003epartner\u0027s parent or step-parent\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003esibling or step-sibling\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003echild or stepchild who is 18 or older and not dependent on you\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003echild or stepchild who is under 18 and not in your or your partner\u0027s daily care and control\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe don\u0027t consider how much contact you have with someone when we decide whether they are your near relative.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e \n\u003cbr\u003e \u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Near-relative"},{"id":104,"title":"Offshore resource activities","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass73D1E24A40A348E383B927FF97CF04DA\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e​An offshore resource activity\u0026#160;is linked to 2 pieces of legislation, the \u003ca href=\"https\u0026#58;//www.legislation.gov.au/Series/C2006A00014\"\u003e\u003cem\u003eOffshore Petroleum and Greenhouse Gas Storage Act 2006\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/a\u003e and the \u003ca href=\"https\u0026#58;//www.legislation.gov.au/Details/C2016C01031\"\u003e\u003ci\u003eOffshore Minerals Act 1994\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/a\u003e. An operation or activity performed under either of these Acts is an offshore resources activity unless excluded by a determination made by the Minister.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Offshore-resource-activities"},{"id":102,"title":"Ordinarily resident","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass5D4C0097D61D4497B1A4941E1C29F3E8\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe may consider you to be ordinarily resident in Australia if your permanent home is in Australia. This is even if you are temporarily absent from Australia.\u0026#160;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou cannot be ordinarily resident in Australia if you are in Australia for a special purpose and you were\u0026#58;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003ein Australia as a child of foreign diplomats or administrative staff who were entitled to diplomatic privileges and immunities\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ein Australia as a child of United Nations staff posted to Australia\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eremoved from Australia after breaching visa conditions or having had a visa cancelled.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Ordinarily-resident"},{"id":125,"title":"Ordinarily resident - 10 year rule","definition":"\u003cp\u003eIf you are born in Australia and claiming to be an Australian citizen on your tenth birthday, you must show that you were ordinarily resident in Australia throughout the first 10 years from your birth. We will consider the circumstances of your whole family to determine if you were ordinarily resident throughout the 10-year period.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe may consider you to\u0026#160;be ordinarily resident in Australia if throughout the first 10 years from your birth, your permanent home is in Australia. This is even if you are temporarily absent from Australia.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe cannot consider you to be ordinarily resident for the 10-year period, if you were in Australia for a special purpose and you were\u0026#58;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003ein Australia as a child of foreign diplomats or administrative staff who were entitled to diplomatic privileges and immunities\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ein Australia as a child of United Nations staff posted to Australia\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eremoved from Australia with your family after breaching visa conditions or having had a visa cancelled.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Ordinarily-resident---10-year-rule"},{"id":109,"title":"Ownership interest","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass7BF779DD36A948BE9603539AB4A1B6CF\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eOwnership interest in relation to a business, means an interest in the business as\u0026#58;\u0026#160;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003ea shareholder in a company that carries on the business, or\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ea partner in a partnership that carries on the business, or\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ethe sole proprietor of the business\u0026#160;including such an interest held indirectly through one or more interposed companies, partnerships or trusts\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Ownership-interest"},{"id":59,"title":"Panel clinic","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClassA6290CE54E254D998D8C65257AAF1890\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eA panel clinic is a clinic that can conduct health examinations\u0026#160;for Australian immigration purposes. Most panel clinics can take x-rays as well.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eFind your nearest panel clinic at \n      \u003ca href=\"/help-support/contact-us/offices-and-locations\"\u003eour locations\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Panel-clinic"},{"id":58,"title":"Panel physician","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass8FF1D3A04D744EA58118E909D21078E2\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eA panel physician is a doctor or radiologist the Australian Government has approved as a member of the immigration panel. Panel physicians perform health examinations for visa applicants who apply for a visa\u0026#160;outside Australia.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Panel-physician"},{"id":47,"title":"Partner","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass2D8036674AA141AD8A2DD0766BF675CF\"\u003eYour partner is your spouse or de facto partner of the same or opposite sex. You can be\u0026#58;\u0026#160; \r\n   \u003cdiv\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003ein a married relationship\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ein a \r\n            \u003ca href=\"/help-support/glossary?expand=true#de-facto\"\u003eDe facto\u003c/a\u003e relationship\u0026#160;\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv\u003eWe will recognise only 1 partnership.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Partner"},{"id":129,"title":"Payer","definition":"\u003cp\u003eFor a refund of a visa application charge - payments are generally made to the person who originally paid the visa application charge (VAC). We call this person the \u003cstrong\u003e\u003cem\u003epayer\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe original payer is recorded in the payment section of the VAC receipt.\u003c/p\u003e​\u003cbr\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Payer"},{"id":28,"title":"Permanent resident","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass41E227E490A2460C8A3E6E802AD766C7\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe definition of permanent resident varies\u0026#160;for visa or citizenship purposes.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":true,"hash":"Permanent-resident"},{"id":132,"title":"Personal identifiers","definition":"\u003cp\u003e‘Personal Identifiers’ are defined in section 5A of the \u003cem\u003eMigration Act 1958\u003c/em\u003e and in section 10 of the \u003cem\u003eAustralian Citizenship Act 2007\u003c/em\u003e as any of the following (including in digital form)\u0026#58;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003efingerprints or handprints of a person (including those taken using paper and ink or digital livescanning technologies)\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ea measurement of a person’s height and weight\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ea photograph or other image of a person’s face\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ean iris scan\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ea person’s signature\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eany other identifier prescribed by the regulations (except an identifier the obtaining of which would involve the carrying out of an intimate forensic procedure within the meaning of section 23WA of the \u003cem\u003eCrimes Act 1914\u003c/em\u003e).\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Personal-identifiers"},{"id":52,"title":"Police certificates","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClassC9D488C844F14B48B63BDF4848B8AB38\"\u003ePolice certificates are official documents issued by a nation\u0027s law enforcement body.\n   \u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":true,"hash":"Police-certificates"},{"id":130,"title":"Primary applicant","definition":"\u003cp\u003eIn a visa application the primary applicant is the person seeking to satisfy the primary criteria for grant of the visa. \u003c/p\u003e​\u003cbr\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Primary-applicant"},{"id":101,"title":"Priority resettlement country","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClassD594D4CC87A846FAB7DE6DB7849336CC\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e​Work in progress\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Priority-resettlement-country"},{"id":108,"title":"Qualifying business","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClassD6FF5393E564498A9E7FB3FF8CE77728\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eQualifying business means an enterprise that\u0026#58;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eis operated for the purpose of making profit through the provision of goods, services or goods and services (other than the provision of rental property) to the public; and\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eis not operated primarily or substantially for the purpose of speculative or passive investment.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e \n   \n\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Qualifying-business"},{"id":120,"title":"Queueing","definition":"\u003cp\u003e\r\n   \u003ca href=\"/help-support/glossary?expand=true#capping-and-queueing\"\u003ecapping and queueing\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Queueing"},{"id":111,"title":"Recognised standard","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass56887976A1294201A833AF7D897BAEFA\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe meaning of recognised standard depends on the visa you are applying for.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":true,"hash":"Recognised-standard"},{"id":85,"title":"Relative","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass04CF8D3B73994174B70B2C9138727946\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eYour relative is\u0026#58;\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eyour partner, child, parent, brother, sister, stepchild, step-parent, stepbrother or stepsister\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eyour grandparent, grandchild, aunt, uncle, niece, nephew or step equivalent\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Relative"},{"id":117,"title":"Relevant offence","definition":"\u003cp\u003e​A relevant offence is an offence against a law, either in Australia or overseas, involving\u0026#58;\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e​violence, including murder, assault, sexual assault or the threat of violence\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eharassment, molestation, intimidation or stalking\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ethe breach of an apprehended violence or similar order\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003efirearms or other dangerous weapons\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003epeople smuggling\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e​human trafficking, slavery\u0026#160;or slavery-like practices (including forced marriage), kidnapping or unlawful confinement\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eattempting to commit\u0026#160;any\u0026#160;of these offences\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eaiding, abetting, counsellin​g or procuring such offences​​.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e​​\u003cbr\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Relevant-offence"},{"id":6,"title":"Responsible parent","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass30B5549D3A1945248C005E8389446E75\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eUnder the\u0026#160;\u003cem data-redactor-tag=\"em\"\u003eAustralian Citizenship Act 2007\u003c/em\u003e, you are the responsible parent of a child if\u0026#58;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eyou are the child\u0027s parent, unless a Family Court order has removed your parental responsibility\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ethe child is to live with you under a parenting order, whether you are their parent or not\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eyou have parental\u0026#160;responsibility\u0026#160;for the child\u0027s long-term or day-to-day care\u0026#160;under a Family Court order, whether you are their parent or not\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eyou have sole or joint guardianship or custody of the child under an Australian or foreign law, including by adoption, operation of law,\u0026#160;court order or otherwise.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Responsible-parent"},{"id":5,"title":"Round trip cruise","definition":"\u003cp\u003eA round trip cruise is one that\u0026#58;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003estarts and ends in Australia\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003elasts up to 30 days.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe time you spend on a round trip cruise counts as time in Australia for your visa, as long as\u0026#58;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eyou remain a passenger during the cruise\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eyou do not go to a foreign country except for transit purposes\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eit lasts no more than 30 days.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eAsk your cruise operator or travel agent if we consider your cruise to be a round trip cruise before embarking on your cruise.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eIf your cruise has ‘round trip cruise’ status, we will treat the time that a person spends on a round trip cruise as if they were still in Australia for the purposes of their visa.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eA round trip cruise will not reset your stay period on your visa and you should check that you have sufficient time on your visa for the total time you intend to stay in Australia.\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eIf the cruise does not have round trip cruise status, you should check that you have a visa that will allow you to return to Australia, especially if your temporary visa has a single travel facility.\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Round-trip-cruise"},{"id":131,"title":"Secondary applicant","definition":"\u003cp\u003eIn a visa application, the secondary applicant is a member of the family unit of the primary applicant, such as their spouse or de facto partner and/or dependent children.\u003c/p\u003e​\u003cbr\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Secondary-applicant"},{"id":37,"title":"Settled","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClassBA11943430584229B638FAF8016B1BE9\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe consider you settled if you\u0026#58;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003ehave lived lawfully in Australia for a reasonable period (usually at least 2 years) and\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eare an Au​stralian citizen, Australian permanent resident or\u0026#160;\u003ca href=\"/help-support/glossary?expand=true#eligible-new-zealand-citizen\"\u003eeligible New Zealand citizen\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn compassionate and compelling circumstances, we might consider Australian citizens to be settled after 3 months.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n   \u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Settled"},{"id":16,"title":"Sibling","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClassFA86A79B736645A6A9F33C29E42E3F72\"\u003e\u003cp\u003e​Your sibling is someone who has at least one parent in common with you.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Sibling"},{"id":123,"title":"Significant criminal record","definition":"\u003cp\u003eYou have a significant criminal record in relation to a relevant offence(s) if you have been sentenced to\u0026#58;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003edeath or imprisonment for life\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ea term of imprisonment of 12 months or more; or\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003etwo or more terms of imprisonment, where the total of those terms is 12 months or more.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Significant-criminal-record"},{"id":77,"title":"Significant medical condition","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClassA18810FB688A450E9B44BA0D04CE3697\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eThere are no diseases or health conditions that automatically mean you won\u0027t meet the health requirement. However, the diseases which most commonly result in permanent visa applicants failing the health requirement are\u0026#58;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eintellectual impairment\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eHIV infection\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003efunctional impairment\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003erenal disease or failure\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ecancer\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Significant-medical-condition"},{"id":69,"title":"Spouse","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass95E458E2B07B437F947E06E25766FD44\"\u003e\u003cdiv\u003eA spouse is one of two people in a married relationship if they are married to each other under a marriage that is valid for the purposes of the Migration Act and\u0026#58;\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\r\n   \u003cdiv\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003ethey have a mutual commitment to a shared life as a married couple to the\u0026#160;exclusion of\u0026#160;all others; and\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ethe relationship between them is genuine and continuing; and\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ethey\u0026#160;live together; \r\n            \u003cstrong\u003eor \u003c/strong\u003e​do not live separately and apart on a permanent basis.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cp\u003eA spouse can be someone of the same or different sex. \r\n      \u003cbr\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":true,"hash":"Spouse"},{"id":10,"title":"Stateless","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClassE5CDC0DAE3F94CF6A74277D2B81D0F75\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eA stateless person is a person who is not considered a national by any state under the operation of its law.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Stateless"},{"id":71,"title":"Stepchild","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass2E1BAAD3AFBE4A4C87DD717EE188F7C1\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eA stepchild is the child of your current or former partner.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf the stepchild is the child of your former partner they must be under 18, and you\u0026#160;must have either\u0026#58;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003ean Australian parenting order that is in force, saying that you are to live with them and look after them\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eguardianship or custody of the child under the law, Australian or otherwise\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Stepchild"},{"id":99,"title":"Subsequent entrant","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass0ABC115772C046F2A916DF3F5C88E0DB\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eSome visas allow your eligible family members to\u0026#160;apply to join you in Australia as subsequent entrants\u0026#160;after you have been granted your visa.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e  \u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Subsequent-entrant"},{"id":18,"title":"Subsequent temporary application charge","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass4999EFCCCFB84E3DA23B5EA76BDC0D7C\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eSome temporary visas attract a subsequent temporary application charge. It\u0026#160;is in addition to any other visa charges you pay when you lodge your visa.\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n   \u003cbr\u003e \n\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":true,"hash":"Subsequent-temporary-application-charge"},{"id":22,"title":"Substantial criminal record","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClassD5C95631A32D4A5DAE11898291E10672\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eA substantial criminal record is based on the length of a sentence imposed by a court of law.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":true,"hash":"Substantial-criminal-record"},{"id":64,"title":"Substantive visa","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass7826B1412AC443A2B618846FE5521F65\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eA substantive visa is any visa that allows the visa holder to remain temporarily in Australia other than\u0026#58;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003ea bridging visa\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ea criminal justice or enforcement visa\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Substantive-visa"},{"id":128,"title":"Unnecessary at the time it was made","definition":"\u003cp\u003eFor a refund of a visa application charge - an application that was unnecessary at the time it was made is where the applicant did not need to apply for a visa to travel to, or stay in Australia.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cbr\u003e","ismoredetails":true,"hash":"Unnecessary-at-the-time-it-was-made"},{"id":45,"title":"Usually resident","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass41C01748546349DFBD9EAABCE0828A49\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou are \u0027usually resident\u0027 at the place that you physically live (eat and sleep) and want to make your home.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Usually-resident"},{"id":7,"title":"Volunteer work","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClassDA82D8BCB1834773B2555027EFC45B70\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eVolunteer work is work that\u0026#58;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eis unpaid (you can be provided with meals, accommodation or out-of-pocket living expenses)\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ewould not otherwise be done by an Australian for pay\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eis short term\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eis incidental to your visit to Australia\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eis done for a not-for-profit organisation\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003ebenefits the community\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\n  \n\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Volunteer-work"},{"id":8,"title":"Work","definition":"\u003cdiv class=\"ExternalClass29D254225D84458FB12A8EC3BF5C0994\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eWork is performing an activity, in Australia , that\u0026#160;a person would normally be remunerated for. This could be payment or some other form of reward.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eFor further information on what activities are permitted on your visa, refer to \r\n      \u003ca href=\"https\u0026#58;//immi.homeaffairs.gov.au/visas/already-have-a-visa/check-visa-details-and-conditions/conditions-list\" target=\"_blank\"\u003evisa co​nditions.​\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e \r\n  ​\r\n\u003c/div\u003e","ismoredetails":false,"hash":"Work"}],"languagePickerItems":[],"multilingualUIElements":[],"configItems":[{"product":"Internet.MasterPage","key":"BetaMessage","value":" \u003cdiv class=\"logo\"\u003e\n  \u003cimg src=\"/style%20library/dist/assets/images/logo-ha.png\" alt=\"Logo\" class=\"img-responsive\" /\u003e\n  \u003c/div\u003e\n \u003ch2\u003eThis is a test website (beta)\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"popup-text\"\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePlease note that the website is in test phase and new content will be progressively added when available. We will continue to update the content and design based on public feedback.\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\nBefore proceeding, please take a moment to review the important \u003ca href=\"/Pages/Conditions-of-use.aspx\" target=\"_blank\"\u003elegal information\u003c/a\u003e about the use of the test website.\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e"},{"product":"Internet.MasterPage","key":"ExternalPopupMessage","value":"\n               \u003ch2\u003eExternal link\u003c/h2\u003e                    \n                \u003cdiv class=\"popup-text\"\u003e\n                  \u003cp\u003eThis is an external link.\u003c/p\u003e\n                \u003c/div\u003e\n"},{"product":"Internet.Search","key":"CustomSearch","value":"/sitesearch?k="},{"product":"Internet.Search","key":"PopularSearchTermsJson","value":"    {\"popularsearch\":[\r\n    { \"site\":\"/\", \"keywords\":[ \"Visa\", \"Citizenship\", \"Form 80\", \"Form 888\"] },\r\n    { \"site\":\"/Visa-subsite\", \"keywords\":[ \"457\", \"600\", \"Business Visa\", \"Family Visa\", \"Visit Visa\" ] },\r\n    { \"site\":\"/Changes-situati